   124	**arrays)` in batches of B = 32 turns. The binding preflights every header
   125	before it writes anything, and a failure names the offending `env`. **An
   126	encoder error on a real recorded state is fail-fast**: stop the episode and
   127	report the episode, turn, field and error. Every turn is a real recorded state, so any
   128	rejection is a 1.3 envelope finding to fix or record, not a row to drop. (The
   129	reference encoded only its 158,772 admitted states; encoding rejected turns too
   130	is a deliberate, stricter difference, needed because step E reads its plan
   131	inputs from these rows.) After each batch, run
   132	`KaggricultureObsBatch.check_contract()` on the torch views, then keep the rows until step E
   133	decides admission, and copy the admitted rows out before the buffers are reused.
