   179	Category mapping. The rows are the reference's first-rejection totals; the new
   180	text is the grammar's message prefix.
   181	
   182	| Reference first rejection | Pairs | New grammar prefix (`grammar.rs`) |
   183	|---|---:|---|
   184	| `unknown market command` | 14,007 | `unknown market command` |
   185	| `unsupported unit command arguments` | 5,621 | `unsupported unit command arguments` |
   186	| `target violates syntax mask: market_item` | 1,668 | `market item syntax` |
   187	| `extra hand commands` | 1,102 | `extra hand commands` |
   188	| `market queue exceeds configured limit` | 17 | `market queue limit` |
   189	| `quantity must be an integer in 0..1023` | 1 | `quantity range` |
   190	
   191	The vocabularies, slot widths, item masks, the unit-quantity ≥ 1 rule and the
   192	hire rule (`actors + hires < hire_limit`) match the reference codec. The check
   193	*order* differs. The reference built every frame and then applied its masks.
   194	`grammar::encode` checks keys, then hand count, then queue length, then each
   195	unit, then each market order, then `validate_program`. A pair with two defects
   196	can therefore change category, but it cannot change admission.
   197	
   198	**F. Shard write.** Write each episode as it completes. Nothing is
   199	concatenated across the corpus (the reference held whole episodes of flat
   200	features in memory).
   201	
   202	## Shard format consumed by `train_bc.py` (5.2)
   203	
   204	Schema id **`kaggriculture-bc-shard-v1`**. Each episode is one
   205	`np.savez_compressed` file at `OUT/<split>/<day>-<episode_id>.npz`. T is the
   206	number of admitted turns in that episode.
   207	
   208	| Array | dtype | shape | Note |
   209	|---|---|---|---|
   210	| `schema` | `<U` 0-d | `()` | `"kaggriculture-bc-shard-v1"`; the loader rejects anything else, including old `features/context` shards |
   211	| 28 observation fields | contract dtype (int64 / float32 / float64 banks / bool) | `[T,2,…]` | names, shapes and dtypes exactly as `_SCHEMA` |
   212	| `can_act` | bool | `[T,2,252]` | loads into `KaggricultureActionMask` |
   213	| `tokens` | int64 | `[T,2,252,12]` | full STOP-terminated program, zero tail |
   214	| `lengths` | int64 | `[T,2]` | frames including STOP |
   215	| `turn` | int64 | `[T]` | original index t; rejected gaps stay visible |
   216	
   217	Seat axis index 0/1 is the recorded seat. Each row is that seat's own view,
   218	with player token 0 as self. There is no rival-private data, episode ID,
   219	opponent name or seed in any array. Tokens are stored at the contract's int64
   220	dtype. A loader may compact them in memory only through a lossless,
   221	range-checked cast declared in its own code, and must cast back to int64
   222	before `evaluate_actions`.
   223	
   224	Dense size is about 282 KB of observation plus 48 KB of tokens per paired
   225	turn, so roughly **52 GB for 158,772 turns**, mostly zero padding. The GPU pod
   226	has about 25 GB of free pod disk (plan "Resource fit"). Compression is
   227	therefore required, and the first pod step measures the compressed bytes and
   228	the load time on one episode. Residency (host memory versus GPU) and the rank
   229	split belong to 5.2. The reference used `[rank::world]` rows per file.
   230	
   231	5.1 makes no value-target decision. The reference `train_bc.py` froze the
   232	critic. 5.2 decides the critic treatment by Isaiah's convention and records
   233	the choice. For that, the manifest carries each episode's `terminal_banks`
   234	(`rewards`), and seat order is structural.
   235	
   236	## Episode-identity split
   237	
   238	The split is per episode, taken from `selection.json`. All turns of an episode
   239	go to its split directory. Before writing, prepare re-checks that no basename
   240	appears in both splits, and that `info.EpisodeId` equals the basename.
   241	Validation (28 episodes, 18,937 admitted turns in the reference) is the only
   242	held-out NLL source for L9 early stopping in 5.2. Selection by held-out NLL is
   243	a selection result, not held-out qualification.
   244	
   245	## Custody manifest
   246	
   247	`OUT/manifest.json` is strict JSON, and a loader validates its keys:
   248	
   249	- run: schema id, `git rev-parse HEAD`, `Cargo.lock` and `uv.lock` SHA-256,
   250	  SHA-256 of the built `owl.rs` extension file, observation schema 3,
   251	  contract document v4, grammar tables version 1, `hire_limit` 241, the
   252	  command line and the worker count;
   253	- source bytes: path, bytes and SHA-256 of every Python file the run executed
   254	  from the checkout (every `sys.modules` entry whose `__file__` lies under the
   255	  repository root, which includes `prepare.py`, the allocator and
   256	  `reference_admission.py`), of `select_replays.py` as run for selection, and
   257	  of the exported reference `actor_codec.py` (which must equal its pinned
   258	  `88ed3d44…40e5d6`);
   259	- source: volume `4llk4uaf20`, source root, the selected ZIP's SHA-256 and
   260	  path, the `selection.json` SHA-256;
   261	- per episode: member, `episode_id`, split, `source_sha256`, bytes,
   262	  `info_seed`, `terminal_banks`, `paired_turns` (719), `admitted`,
   263	  first-rejection counts, per-seat rejection counts, normalization counts,
   264	  shard path, shard SHA-256 and bytes;
   265	- totals by split.
   266	
   267	**Source identity.** A HEAD and a dirty flag cannot identify modified
   268	preparation, allocator or oracle code, so a dirty run is refused, not
   269	flagged. On both execution routes (data pod and GPU-pod fallback), selection
   270	and preparation run from an immutable clean checkout of the committed
   271	revision: a fresh clone or a dedicated worktree, never a shared working tree
   272	that a learner or an operator may edit. At start, `prepare.py` requires
   273	`git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` to be empty and records HEAD
   274	and the source-byte hashes above. Before publishing `manifest.json` it
   275	re-checks: HEAD unchanged, the tree still clean, every recorded file's
   276	SHA-256 unchanged, and the extension hash unchanged. Any mismatch is a hard
   277	error and no manifest is written. `OUT` lies outside the checkout, so the
   278	run's own output cannot dirty it.
   279	
   280	**What is tracked.** Shard NPZ bulk and `manifest.json` stay out of git. The
   281	committed receipt in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/5.1/` holds a compact
   282	**per-shard custody inventory** (`shard-inventory.json`: for each of the 252
   283	shards its path relative to `OUT`, split, bytes and SHA-256, plus the same
   284	three fields for `manifest.json`), as the
   285	[custody Decision](../../../cookbook/decisions/evaluation-preserves-generality-and-evidence.md)
   286	requires for local bulk artifacts. It also holds the totals, the acceptance
   287	diff and the logs.
   288	
