ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.4.md:44:- **L6 reuse fence (Claude review R1).** One buffer set, no generations. At the entry of `reset`, `step` and `truncate_envs`, before the native call, the adapter calls `torch.cuda.current_stream(transfer_device).synchronize()` when `transfer_device.type == "cuda"` and the buffers are pinned. That is exactly the condition under which ppo.py issues nonblocking copies (W:python/owl/train/ppo.py:561–563). Every read of env buffers in ppo.py and run_ppo.py is enqueued on the current stream before the next env call, and the code base has no side streams (`grep` for `cuda.Stream`/`Event(`/`wait_stream` finds none). So this is an explicit fence, not reliance on the blocking action transfer (ppo.py:2273–2281, 2301). CPU or unpinned runs make no CUDA call. A future reader on another stream must join the current stream before the env call. No trainer API is added.
